  BEFORE: Consider another argument for the possibility of moral observation. Michael Moore argues that since moral properties are natural properties (per his ethical naturalist stance), and since we may be able to perceive the relevant natural properties, we can therefore perceive moral properties. In short, Moore takes the following argument to be valid:

I can perceive $N$.

Good $= N$

Therefore, I can perceive goodness.[36]
  AFTER:  Consider another argument for the possibility of moral observation. Michael Moore argues that since moral properties are natural properties (per his ethical naturalist stance), and since we may be able to perceive the relevant natural properties, we can therefore perceive moral properties. In short, Moore takes the following argument to be valid:

